  "title": "BRAR_NQ",
  "description": "BRAR_NQ is a neuroimaging dataset investigating the neural correlates of Quranic recitation through magnetoencephalography (MEG) recordings. The dataset explores the brain's reward and anti-reward circuitry during exposure to melodic recitation of the Noble Quran, combining MEG neuroimaging to map neural activity patterns associated with this unique auditory-linguistic stimulus.",
